---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
import Command from '../components/Command.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import evidence from '../data/evidence.json';

const sample = evidence.servers.find((server) => server.ref.includes('sequential-thinking'));
---
<Base
  title="Verify an MCP server"
  description="An MCP server can annotate a tool readOnlyHint: true and nothing checks it. rigorrun verify pins the server to the bytes the registry published, runs it in a container with no network, exercises every tool it safely can, and reports what actually changed."
>
  <Section>
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_1fr] lg:gap-16">
      <div>
        <Eyebrow>One command, no project</Eyebrow>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-display font-medium text-balance">
          Find out what a server’s tools actually do.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-lead text-secondary">
          An MCP server can annotate a tool <span class="font-mono text-support">readOnlyHint: true</span>.
          Nothing checks that. Agents use it to decide whether a tool can be called without asking
          you first.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-support text-secondary">
          RigorRun fetches the server, pins it to the exact bytes the registry published, runs it in a
          container with no network and no access to your machine, calls each tool with arguments
          derived from its own schema, and reads the filesystem before and after to see what actually
          changed. Then it compares that with what the server declared about itself.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8">
          <Command command="rigorrun verify npm:@modelcontextprotocol/server-memory@2026.8.31" />
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-support text-muted">
          No project, no browser, no agent, nothing to configure first. Needs Docker, because every
          server runs in a container that is thrown away afterwards.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div data-theme="ink" class="rounded-panel border border-line bg-canvas p-5" data-reveal>
        <pre class="overflow-x-auto font-mono text-meta leading-relaxed text-fg" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Example output of rigorrun verify"><code>{`resolve    npm:@modelcontextprotocol/server-memory@2026.8.31
stage      installing with lifecycle scripts disabled
isolation  measuring whether reset actually resets
discover   ${sample?.toolsDiscovered ?? 9} tool(s)

digest     ${(sample?.digest ?? '').slice(0, 46)}…
isolation  RESET
egress     none

Declared, versus what it did
tool                declared              result    verification
-----------------   -------------------   -------   ------------
sequentialthinking  readOnlyHint: true    CONFORMS  PARTIAL
sequentialthinking  destructiveHint:false CONFORMS  PARTIAL
sequentialthinking  idempotentHint: true  CONFORMS  PARTIAL

Every discovered tool was exercised.`}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section ruled tight>
    <h2 class="text-display font-medium">What each exit code means</h2>
    <dl class="mt-10 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-panel border border-line bg-line sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {
        [
          ['0', 'Verified', 'Every claim it could check held, and nothing was contradicted.'],
          ['1', 'Contradicted', 'A declaration the server made about itself was contradicted by what it was observed to do.'],
          ['3', 'Too little', 'It ran, and established too little to be worth much. Fewer tools were reachable than you asked for.'],
          ['2', 'Harness failed', 'Something in the setup or the runtime broke. Never a finding about the server, and never dressed up as one.'],
        ].map(([code, title, body]) => (
          <div class="bg-surface p-5">
            <dt class="flex items-baseline gap-2.5">
              <span class="font-mono text-metric font-medium text-accent">{code}</span>
              <span class="text-section font-semibold">{title}</span>
            </dt>
            <dd class="mt-2 text-support text-secondary">{body}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>

    <div class="mt-8 rounded-panel border border-line bg-raised p-6">
      <p class="max-w-3xl text-support text-secondary">
        <span class="text-fg">Nothing it could not establish is reported as a fact.</span> A tool it
        could not exercise safely is listed with the reason, and a record that omits what it could not
        reach is not a cleaner record — it is a false one. Run against
        {' '}{evidence.totals.servers} published servers, it exercised {evidence.totals.toolsExercised}
        {' '}of {evidence.totals.toolsDiscovered} tools; the rest are named rather than rounded away.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6"><Button href="/evidence" variant="secondary">Read the full record</Button></div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
